<ToolPage current="/dice-roller/" title="Roll Dice Online: Free Virtual Dice Roller (d6, d20 & More) | Who Goes First?" description="Roll up to 12 virtual dice online: d4, d6, d8, d10, d12, d20 or d100. Fair, instant and free, with the total added up. For board games when the dice go missing." heading="Roll dice" lede="Lost the dice? Pick how many and how many sides, then roll.">
  <DiceRoller client:load />
  <Fragment slot="about">
    <h2>Using dice to pick who goes first</h2>
    <p>Many rulebooks say the highest roller starts. Everyone rolls in turn and the highest total goes first; players who tie roll again. To skip the rerolls, the <a href="/methods/dice/">dice reveal in the picker</a> rolls for the whole table at once and never ties.</p>
    <h2>Are these dice fair?</h2>
    <p>Each die is an independent draw from your browser’s secure random number generator, so every face has exactly the same chance. Unlike real dice, there are no worn edges or lucky throws.</p>
    <h2>Which dice to pick</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Two six-sided dice (2d6)</strong> for most family board games, including Catan, Monopoly and backgammon.</li>
      <li><strong>One d20</strong> for many role-playing games, or as a quick 1–20 tie-breaker with a low chance of ties.</li>
      <li><strong>d4, d8, d10 and d12</strong> for role-playing damage rolls and some dice games.</li>
      <li><strong>d100</strong> for percentile rolls, where 1 to 100 reads as a percentage.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can roll up to 12 dice of the same type at once. The total is added up for you, and each die is shown separately so you can still read single values.</p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <h3>Why does a total of 7 come up so often with two dice?</h3>
    <p>Because more combinations make 7 than any other total: 1+6, 2+5, 3+4, 4+3, 5+2 and 6+1. That is 6 of the 36 equally likely pairs, or 1 in 6. A 2 or a 12 can only happen one way, so each has a 1 in 36 chance.</p>
    <h3>Can I roll different dice together, like a d20 and a d6?</h3>
    <p>Roll them one type at a time: choose the d20, roll, then switch to d6 and roll again.</p>
    <p>Not sure what your game says? <a href="/games/">Look up its official starting rule</a>.</p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolPage>
